# Technology Stack — Approved Libraries Only

<ABSOLUTE_RULE>
No new library may be added to the codebase without explicit approval.
If a task seems to require a library not on this list, ASK before adding it.
</ABSOLUTE_RULE>

## Core Stack

| Layer              | Library                    | Purpose                                    |
|-------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Language          | Python 3.12                | Latest stable, best async performance      |
| Web Framework     | FastAPI                    | Async-native API layer                     |
| HTTP Client       | httpx (HTTP/2)             | All fetch_ functions — async, pooled       |
| Serialisation     | msgspec                    | JSON encode/decode — unconditionally       |
| Event Loop        | uvloop                     | 2–4× faster asyncio                        |
| Live State Cache  | Redis + redis.asyncio      | Provider cache, agent status, TTL, 24h hot cache |
| Historical Store  | PostgreSQL + asyncpg       | Signal history, agent verdicts, trade log  |
| Vector Store      | Qdrant (primary) + LanceDB (hot standby) | Semantic retrieval, RAG memory |
| Embeddings        | MistralEmbeddingClient     | Interim — local Qwen planned               |
| Data Processing   | Polars                     | Time-series OHLCV — never Pandas           |
| Data Models       | Pydantic v2 (frozen)       | All schemas, validation                    |
| Config            | pydantic-settings (`PolarisSettings`) | Typed env var management — only source of config |
| Logging           | Loguru                     | Structured logs (positional syntax only)   |
| LLM Observability | Langfuse (self-hosted)     | LLM tracing, SDK ≥3.0                      |
| Infra Metrics     | prometheus_client          | Redis/PostgreSQL/HTTP metrics — NOT for LLM tracing |
| Type Checker      | pyright                    | `mypy` is banned                           |
| Testing           | pytest + pytest-asyncio    | Unit + smoke tests, async-native           |

